            'The curvatura major and minor do not only differ in length; the ligamentous/peritoneal connections and the courses of the vessels are also related to these borders. The lesser curvature is related to the lesser omentum towards the liver and the greater curvature to the greater omentum and neighbouring connections. The pancreas behind the stomach is not a direct continuation of the stomach lumen; it delivers its secretion to the duodenum by way of a duct. Neighbourhood of organs and connection for the passage of contents must be distinguished.',
