            'Among the anterior neighbours the diaphragm, the left lobe of the liver and the anterior abdominal wall; among the posterior relationships the pancreas through the bursa omentalis and the structures of the posterior abdomen are important. The spleen is near the upper region of the greater curvature and the transverse colon is in a more inferior relationship. The fullness of the stomach and the build of the person change the surface projection. The lesser and greater curvatures are considered together with the vascular arches and the omental connections; the surrounding ligaments are not only mechanical suspension but peritoneal folds carrying the vascular routes.',
